-- title:
--   Quotient formal mathcal O_D-module along invariant coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring in which $p$ is nilpotent, and let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$ in the project's sense: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ over $B$ together with series $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ ($a$ in the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{p^2}$) and $X.\varpi$, each a law endomorphism of $X.F$, with $\mathrm{act}\,1$ the identity, $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive (composition, resp. addition via $X.F$), $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}\,a=\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{Frob}\,a)\circ\varpi$. Let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ and $h\in\mathbb N$, subject to: $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is a finite projective $B$-module; for every field $\kappa$ and ring map $f:B\to\kappa$ the $\kappa$-dimension of $\kappa[\![x]\!]/I\kappa[\![x]\!]$ is $p^h$; some power $x_i^q$ lies in $I$ for both $i$; every element of $I$ has zero constant term; for $f\in I$, $f(X.F(x,y))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $I(x)\cup I(y)$; and $I$ is stable under substitution of each $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ and of $X.\varpi$. Let $u=(u_1,u_2)$ be a pair of power series with zero constant terms such that $u_j(X.F(x,y))-u_j(x)$ lies in the ideal generated by $I(y)$, such that $u_1,u_2$ generate $I$, and such that every $w\in B[\![x]\!]$ with $w(X.F(x,y))-w(x)$ in the ideal generated by $I(y)$ is $W(u)$ for a unique $W$. Then there is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $Y$ over $B$ with `IsIsogenyOfHeight X Y u h`: $u$ is a law homomorphism $X.F\to Y.F$ commuting with every $\mathrm{act}\,a$ and with $\varpi$, and `HasKernelOfDegree u (p ^ h)` holds, i.e. `KerAlgebra u` is a finite projective $B$-module and for every field $\kappa$ and $f:B\to\kappa$ the $\kappa$-dimension of `KerAlgebra (u.map f)` equals $p^h$.
--
--   This is the construction of the quotient of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module by a finite flat subgroup presented by an ideal $I$ of invariants, in the form in which the quotient comes equipped with its own $\mathcal O_D$-structure and the given invariant coordinates $u$ realise the quotient map as an isogeny of height $h$. It is used to produce covers by isogenies of prescribed height in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_isIsogenyOfHeight_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_isIsogenyOfHeight_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal).
